  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If VRChat implements EAC to block modding, there are 2 enormous problems I can immediately see happening:\n1) Modding communities that work solely to improve the game will be shut out and the positive influence they brought to the game will be lost. Mods have given users a far better game experience, and there are even clients that help protect you from actual malicious mods. That brings me to my next point.\n2) Removing modding will not only do nothing to prevent crasher avatars and malicious clients, it will literally remove the only way for people to PROTECT themselves from them.\nIf VRChat really wants to make their game better for everyone, they must either add mod support (i.e. through steam workshop), or incorporate the QoL and safety features that mods are having to make up for.",
